# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing under data/ is committed by default. It holds two kinds of thing that
# must never be published: personal recordings (EEG is biometric data, and the
# session folders carry the participant's own events) and generated media
# (downloaded or synthesised stimuli, tens of MB, reproducible from the specs).
#
# `data/**` (rather than `data/`) is deliberate: excluding the whole directory
# makes the re-include below impossible, because git cannot re-include a file
# whose parent directory is excluded. This form excludes the contents but lets
# the attribution file through.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/**
!data/stimuli/
!data/stimuli/ATTRIBUTION.md

# raw arrays and binaries
*.npy
*.bin

# secrets and machine-local settings: never commit these
neurobridge.yaml
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# environments and caches
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# trained models and reports are per-machine artifacts
*.joblib
*.pkl

# editors / OS
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
